  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A particle undergoing simple harmonic motion has time\r\n\r\ndependent displacement given by $x(t)=\\mathrm{A} \\sin \\frac{\\pi t}{90}$. The ratio of kinetic to potential energy of this particle at $\\mathrm{t}=210 \\mathrm{~s}$ will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "cZUE7",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{9}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Or6CB",
      "text": "1",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Wh3UH",
      "text": "2",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tmSbU",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Kinetic energy, $\\mathrm{k}=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{~m} \\omega^{2} \\mathrm{~A}^{2} \\cos ^{2} \\omega \\mathrm{t}$\r\n\r\nPotential energy, $U=\\frac{1}{2} m \\omega^{2} A^{2} \\sin ^{2} \\omega t$\r\n\r\n$\\frac{k}{U}=\\cot ^{2} \\omega t=\\cot ^{2} \\frac{\\pi}{90}(210)=\\frac{1}{3}$",
    "image": null
  },
